    <figure class="col-md-6 a-figure mod-text-image__image">
      <picture class="h-ratio h-ratio16-9 h-display-block">



          <img alt="Technology career opportunities" loading="lazy" src="/assets-f/img/baed40fa4ab504.jpg" srcset="/assets-f/img/94fbfa896928ec.jpg 767w, /assets-f/img/baed40fa4ab504.jpg 1400w" sizes="(min-width: 768px) calc(93.75vw/5), (max-width: 767px) 90vw">



      </picture>

      <div class="caption mod-text-image__image__caption">Swisslog offers attractive career opportunities for entry-level professionals, university graduates and professionals.</div>

    </figure>
    <div class="col-md-6 copy mod-text-image__text">

      <div class="a-mod-headline mod-text-image__text__headline">
        <h2>Agile team structures</h2>
      </div>


      <p>We deliver added value for our customers through global team structures. The key elements of our corporate strategy include developing our employees, enhancing cooperation and continuous further education.</p>
<p>If you would like to make a difference, then Swisslog is just the place for you. In our team you can advance technologies while working at the core of digitization and robotics.</p>
<p><a href="#">&gt; &nbsp;Learn more about Swisslog as an employer and job vacancies.</a></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
<article class="mod mod-text" data-ignore="true">

  <span class="js-anchorlink" id="History" data-anchor-title="History"></span>


  <div class="row">
    <div class="col-md-10 col-lg-8 offset-md-1 offset-lg-2">

      <div class="a-mod-headline mod-text__headline">
        <h2> History of Swisslog</h2>
      </div>


      <div class="copy">
        <p style="margin: 0cm 0cm 10pt;"><strong>1900</strong><br>
Swisslog traces its roots back to Sprecher + Schuh AG, founded in the Swiss town of Aarau. Initially, the company’s primary area of activity was energy distribution.</p>
<p><strong>1969</strong><br>
First pallet crane invented, creating the foundation for the <a href="#">Vectura product line.</a></p>
<p><strong>Mid-1980s<br>
</strong>
Core businesses sold to Alstom Group (France) and Rockwell/Allen-Bradley (USA).&nbsp;Company shifts focus to automation technology, acquiring Translift, Digitron, and OWL.</p>
<p><strong>1994</strong><br>
Sprecher + Schuh changes its name to Swisslog, establishing itself as a leading global provider of automation solutions for hospitals, warehouses, and distribution centers.</p>
<p><strong>1996</strong><br>
Swisslog designs the first robotic picking solution.</p>
<p><strong>1998</strong><br>
Swisslog acquires Munck Automation and enters the US market with its Newport News, Virginia office.</p>
<p><strong>2009</strong><br>
Launch of <a href="#">SynQ software</a> and addition of <a href="#">light goods technology</a> to the portfolio.</p>
<p><strong>2010</strong><br>
Swisslog integrates the first <a href="#">AutoStore ASRS solution</a>.</p>
<p><strong>2014</strong><br>
<a href="https://www.kuka.com/en-us">KUKA, a global leader in robotics and automation</a>, acquires Swisslog.</p>
<p><strong>2016</strong><br>
Swisslog acquires FORTE and its light goods expertise, while adding PAS and the <a href="#">PowerStore pallet shuttle system</a>.</p>
<p><strong>2019</strong><br>
<a href="http://www.swisslog-healthcare.com">Swisslog Healthcare</a> becomes an independent brand, focusing on healthcare facilities and hospitals.&nbsp;Swisslog continues expanding in intralogistics, production logistics, and supply chain.</p>
<p><strong>2020</strong><br>
Swisslog supports the surge in <a href="#">e-grocery </a>and <a href="#">e-commerce fulfillment</a> solutions.</p>
<p><strong>2023</strong><br>
Swisslog rebrands to reflect a <a href="#">new era of digital logistics</a>.</p>
<p><strong>2024</strong><br>
Swisslog opens new Americas headquarters in Atlanta, Georgia, and expands its presence in Canada.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</article>
